# C1 Job-specific results: developer notes

- Own view, shown after a Job-specific scan (PRD FR-36). Only a Relevancy Score and a Keyword Gap summary. No four categories. UPDATED: AutoFix and Magic Write work here, because the job description is kept with the scan (FR-54). This view is being redesigned to add a list of lines to tailor.
- Rail: ring with the Relevancy percentage (amber below 75, green only when strong), label "Relevancy score", and the Magic Write row (locked preview for Free).
- Middle panel, Free: headline "You match X of Y keywords from this job description." and four group counts (hard skills, soft skills, job titles/certifications/tools, industry language). The full breakdown is a locked placeholder. Real missing keywords are never sent to the browser for Free.
- CV is plain, with no highlights, because highlights would need the locked breakdown.
- Top bar: mode switch on Job-specific. Free users get 1 Job-specific scan per month.

## Keyword visibility for Free (decided 11 Nov, PRD 12.2 and FR-36)
- Free sees the Relevancy Score, matched and missing counts per group, and the matched keywords as chips.
- Missing keywords: shown only as a count per group ("4 missing") with a PRO lock. Their names are never sent to the browser for Free.
- Above the locked card: "N keywords from the job are missing from your CV. Unlock PRO to see them and add them with Magic Write." N is the real number.